{"apiVersion":"2.2.16","documentationUrl":"https:\/\/jobi.cy\/apidocs","friendlyNotice":"Thanks for using Jobicy API! Please ensure Jobicy is clearly credited with a direct link to the source, and all application buttons redirect to the original job URL provided in this feed. That’s all! You might be building something amazing, we wish you the best of luck!","jobCount":6,"lastUpdate":"2026-08-19T14:48:32+00:00","appliedFilters":{"count":200,"geo":"usa","tag":"operations coordinator"},"jobs":[{"id":151115,"url":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/jobs\/151115-legal-operations-coordinator","jobSlug":"151115-legal-operations-coordinator","jobTitle":"Legal Operations Coordinator","companyName":"Grove Collaborative","companyLogo":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/data\/server-nyc0409\/galaxy\/mercury\/2022\/02\/574531d8dd057e68801193a869098c18.jpeg","jobIndustry":["Legal & Compliance"],"jobType":["Full-Time"],"jobGeo":"USA","jobLevel":"Senior","jobExcerpt":"Grove Collaborative is a sustainability-focused consumer products company creating household and personal care essentials that are effective, beautifully designed, and healthier for people and the planet. We are a certified B Corp, plastic-neutral, and on a mission to transform the CPG industry for good. Temporary Contract for Parental Leave Coverage | September 2026 – January&hellip;","jobDescription":"<p>Grove Collaborative is a sustainability-focused consumer products company creating household and personal care essentials that are effective, beautifully designed, and healthier for people and the planet. We are a certified B Corp, plastic-neutral, and on a mission to transform the CPG industry for good.<\/p>\n<p>Temporary Contract for Parental Leave Coverage | September 2026 – January 2027 | Remote<\/p>\n<p>We are open to a full-time or part-time schedule | $28-34\/hour<\/p>\n<p><strong>THE SHORT VERSION<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>We're looking for an experienced Legal Operations Coordinator to join a three-person legal team at a public company and take ownership of recurring operational workstreams — contracts, e-signature administration, and compliance support — for about five months while our Legal Operations Lead is on maternity leave. Our GC and AGC will set priorities and be available for the genuinely novel calls, but the day-to-day execution is yours to run.<\/p>\n<p>This is a strong fit if you've already built a real foundation in legal operations or paralegal work and are ready to own a workstream independently at a public company, working directly with a GC and AGC who'll trust you to execute without close supervision.<\/p>\n<p><strong>WHAT YOU'LL OWN<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><em>Contracts &amp; Legal Technology<\/em> <\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Own Grove's day-to-day contract lifecycle process end-to-end: intake via Tropic, triage, routing for review, execution, and archiving in Juro — running the process independently and escalating only genuine exceptions. <\/li>\n<li>Administer Grove's e-signature tools (Adobe Acrobat Sign and Google Workspace eSignature), including troubleshooting user issues, as Grove transitions off DocuSign. <\/li>\n<li>Manage Legal's vendor relationships directly: run regular check-ins and track renewal timelines, bringing decisions to counsel only when they call for judgment beyond process.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><em>Compliance &amp; Corporate Governance<\/em> <\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Own SOX process documentation within Legal and cross-functionally — gathering and organizing audit evidence in coordination with Finance and Internal Audit without needing task-level direction. <\/li>\n<li>Maintain the corporate calendar (board meetings, regulatory filing deadlines), track state registrations, and manage filing of completed board minutes. <\/li>\n<li>Run point on the logistics of responses to data requests, subpoenas, or document productions, executing under counsel's direction on strategy.<\/li>\n<li>Monitor adherence to Legal policies and procedures company-wide, flagging gaps proactively rather than waiting to be asked.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><em>Records, Billing &amp; Insurance<\/em> <\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Run Legal's filing systems with discipline — naming conventions, document retention, and legal hold processes — as the person accountable for consistency, not just someone following a checklist. <\/li>\n<li>Own legal billing review: track outside counsel invoices against billing guidelines and flag anomalies for review. <\/li>\n<li>Manage Grove's corporate insurance portfolio, including renewals, purchases, and claims.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>YOUR TOOLKIT<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>You should already be comfortable picking up systems like these quickly — we'll ramp you on Grove's specific setup, not the underlying skill: <\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tropic — Contract intake &amp; procurement workflow <\/li>\n<li>Juro — Contract repository &amp; document management <\/li>\n<li>Adobe Acrobat Sign \/ Google Workspace eSignature — E-signature <\/li>\n<li>Confluence &amp; Jira — Internal wiki, knowledge base, ticketing <\/li>\n<li>Google Workspace — The full suite — Docs, Drive, Sheets, Slides, Gmail, Calendar <\/li>\n<li>Slack — Primary communication channel, company-wide <\/li>\n<li>Claude (Anthropic) — AI assistant for legal workflows — Chat and Cowork<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li> 3–5 years of experience in legal operations, paralegal work, or in-house legal support, with a track record of owning recurring workstreams independently. <\/li>\n<li>Genuine interest in public company legal operations; prior exposure to SOX or corporate governance processes is a strong plus. <\/li>\n<li>Hands-on experience with tools like CLMs, e-signature platforms, or procurement systems — you don't need our specific stack, but you should be well past the learning-the-basics stage. <\/li>\n<li>Bachelor's degree required. Paralegal certificate or coursework is a plus. <\/li>\n<li>Clear, professional communication skills, and comfort driving cross-functional conversations with Finance, Marketing, IT, and Engineering without needing someone else to broker them. <\/li>\n<li>Real comfort using AI tools as part of daily workflow, not just curiosity about them. <\/li>\n<li>A default of discretion and professionalism when handling sensitive or confidential information. <\/li>\n<li>Bonus: familiarity with Tropic, Juro, DataGrail, or similar platforms; background at a tech or e-commerce company.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>WHAT TO EXPECT<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clear priorities and context from our GC and AGC, who set direction and trust you to run execution independently. <\/li>\n<li>A focused onboarding to Grove's specific tools and processes — you bring the underlying experience, we'll handle the specifics. <\/li>\n<li>Real ownership of how legal operations runs at a public company, with guidance available for genuinely novel situations, not routine ones. <\/li>\n<li>A collaborative team that treats legal ops as a strategic function worth investing in.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>WHY THIS GIG<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>You'll get real ownership of public company legal operations workstreams, not busywork. <\/li>\n<li>You'll work directly with a GC and AGC who value legal ops and will treat you as someone who can run with it. <\/li>\n<li>Grove is a Certified B Corp genuinely building a more sustainable consumer economy. The mission is real. <\/li>\n<li>You'll get exposure to how AI tools like Claude are used in daily legal workflows.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>IMPORTANT DETAILS<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>This temporary, non-exempt position is remote for candidates based in the following states: California, Maine, Pennsylvania, Nevada, North Carolina, Texas, Colorado, Washington, Illinois, New York, Missouri, and Massachusetts.<\/p>\n<p>The comp range for this role is<strong> $28-34\/hour. <\/strong>Our compensation bands are determined based on market-specific cost of living data, meaning that <strong>the top of our range is reserved for the most experienced candidates in the highest cost of living areas across the country.<\/strong> This role is not eligible for an annual incentive target or equity.<\/p>\n<p><strong>MORE ABOUT GROVE<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Grove Collaborative Holdings, Inc. (NYSE: GROV) is the one-stop online destination for everyday essentials that create a healthier home and planet. Explore thousands of thoughtfully vetted products for every room and everyone in your home, including household cleaning, personal care, health and wellness, laundry, clean beauty, kitchen, pantry, kids, baby, pet care, and beyond. Everything Grove sells meets a higher standard — from health to sustainability and performance — so you get a great value without compromising your values. As a B Corp and Public Benefit Corporation, Grove goes beyond selling products: every order is carbon neutral, supports plastic waste cleanup initiatives, and lets you see and track the positive impact of your choices. Shopping with purpose starts at <a href=\"http:\/\/grove.com\/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Grove.com<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>We're building a diverse and inclusive work environment where we learn from each other. We welcome people of diverse backgrounds, experiences, abilities and perspectives. We are an equal opportunity employer. If you require reasonable accommodation in completing this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please direct your inquiries to <a href=\"mailto:Talent@grove.co\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Talent@grove.co<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>For information on our privacy policy, visit <a href=\"https:\/\/www.grove.co\/policies\/privacy-policy?srsltid=AfmBOorziG_Let7pnfGS-_BNWxMEhnDkvwfUSAuxZ_8LOcd4bGgvm-wR\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">this link<\/a> on our website. <\/p>","pubDate":"2026-08-19T14:48:32+00:00","salaryMin":28,"salaryMax":34,"salaryCurrency":"USD","salaryPeriod":"hourly"},{"id":152292,"url":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/jobs\/152292-senior-manager-talent-people-operations-claude-corps","jobSlug":"152292-senior-manager-talent-people-operations-claude-corps","jobTitle":"Senior Manager, Talent & People Operations, Claude Corps","companyName":"CodePath","companyLogo":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/data\/server-nyc0409\/galaxy\/mercury\/2026\/06\/58acdc3a-221.webp","jobIndustry":["HR & Recruiting"],"jobType":["Full-Time"],"jobGeo":"USA","jobLevel":"Senior","jobExcerpt":"CodePath is the largest educator of college computer science students in the country. We've trained over 40,000 students from 1,000+ universities, and our partners include Amazon, Google, and other leading technology companies. We've spent nearly a decade training the next generation of technical talent, and we just launched a $150M initiative with Anthropic, building one&hellip;","jobDescription":"<p>CodePath is the largest educator of college computer science students in the country. We've trained over 40,000 students from 1,000+ universities, and our partners include Amazon, Google, and other leading technology companies. We've spent nearly a decade training the next generation of technical talent, and we just launched a $150M initiative with Anthropic, building one of the most ambitious AI workforce programs in the world.<\/p>\n<p>We're now expanding into new markets and scaling our team so we can move at the speed AI is transforming the workforce. People joining CodePath now will have the opportunity to help architect the next frontier of our work.<\/p>\n<p>We believe technical skill is the fastest way to turn raw talent into real opportunity. We train the engineers the AI era runs on, building toward millions of learners, hundreds of millions in revenue, and billions in economic impact. If you want to own something and be part of a 0-to-1 journey at an organization moving at the speed of AI, this is the place to build it.<\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Role<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Location:<\/strong> Remote (U.S.)<\/p>\n<p><strong>Role Type:<\/strong> Full-Time <\/p>\n<p><strong>Reporting to:<\/strong> Head of People<\/p>\n<p><strong>Compensation:<\/strong> $110,000 to $150,000 per year<\/p>\n<p><strong>Manages:<\/strong> A pod of early-talent recruiters plus fractional HR coordination support<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><strong>Key Activities<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Claude Corps is a fellowship that places early-career technologists inside nonprofits, government agencies, and public-interest organizations to build AI solutions that keep working after the fellow leaves. It runs as a partnership between Anthropic, CodePath, and Social Finance, backed by a $150M initiative with Anthropic. CodePath is the Employer of Record: we own the full fellow lifecycle, from recruiting and selection through employment, onboarding, benefits, and host support.<br \/>Cohort 1 places 100 fellows. The program scales toward 1,000 fellows in year one and 10,000 by year three. This role builds the pod that makes that scale real.<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><strong>Why this role, now<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Claude Corps needs one person accountable for how fellows get hired and how they get employed. Not a strategic HR seat at a distance from the work, and not a recruiting manager who hands off at the offer. A pod lead, running a small team that carries both.<\/p>\n<p>You'll manage the recruiters screening early talent, and you'll manage the fractional HR coordination support that turns an accepted offer into a real employee. Where the program touches the person, you and the Claude Corps program managers work the case together: performance concerns, employee relations, a placement that isn't landing. You bring the process and the employment side. They bring the day-to-day context and the host relationship. Both names are on the outcome.<\/p>\n<p>The math is the other half of the job. We go from 100 fellows to 1,000 to 10,000, and the pod does not grow 100x to match. A team this size clears that volume by building AI into the work: screening support, scheduling, candidate communication, onboarding packets, compliance tracking, the reporting that eats a coordinator's week. We train people to build with AI. We expect the people running our own operations to do the same.<br \/>The pod is small in Cohort 1. It grows with the cohorts, and how much it has to grow is partly up to you.<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><strong>What you will own <\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Lead the pod<\/strong>. Manage the fractional early-talent recruiters and the HR coordinators supporting Claude Corps. Set the week's priorities, run the load-balancing when a cohort deadline compresses, coach against the bar, and grow the team's headcount and capability as cohorts scale. Fractional support means you are explicit about what you're buying with those hours and what falls to you.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Own screening and selection<\/strong>. Run the funnel from application review through offer, against the program's selection rubric and calibration process. Keep throughput honest: the pod moves volume, and you hold the line on signal quality and candidate experience while it does.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Own the employer-of-record lifecycle<\/strong>. Offers and e-sign, background checks, I-9 and work authorization, payroll setup, benefits enrollment, onboarding. Fellows are CodePath employees, and the experience should feel like it. You direct this work through the fractional coordinators rather than doing all of it yourself.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Use AI to hold the ratio<\/strong>. Find the repetitive work in recruiting and HR ops and get it automated or AI-assisted: resume screening support, interview scheduling, candidate comms, offer and onboarding document generation, multi-state compliance tracking, cohort reporting. Judgment calls stay with humans, and you decide where that line sits. Come with a bias toward trying things, and bring the team along so the whole pod works this way, not just you.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Co-own employee relations and performance with program management<\/strong>. When a fellow's performance or conduct needs attention, you and the program manager run it together. You own documentation, process, consistency, and the employment decisions that follow. The PM owns the host relationship and what's actually happening on the ground. Escalate to the Head of People when the situation warrants it, and know where that line is.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Build the systems<\/strong>. Turn one-cohort processes into repeatable operations: screening workflows, HR SLAs, multi-state compliance, and clean handoffs with our program partners. Bring a point of view on what to standardize and what to leave flexible while the program is still forming<em><br \/><\/em><\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><strong>Who you are<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li> 5+ years across recruiting and HR or people operations, including time owning both, not just one<\/li>\n<li>You've managed people, and you've managed through others' capacity, including contractors, shared services, or fractional support<\/li>\n<li>You've run high-volume or early-talent hiring, and you've owned HR operations (payroll, benefits, compliance, onboarding). Employer-of-record, PEO, or multi-state employment experience is a strong plus<\/li>\n<li>You already use AI in your own work and can point to something you automated or rebuilt with it. Comfort with ATS and HRIS configuration, workflow automation, and prompting is expected, not a bonus<\/li>\n<li>You've handled employee relations and performance conversations, and you're steady in them<\/li>\n<li>You're comfortable in a program that is still being built. You bring structure without waiting for someone else to hand it to you<\/li>\n<li>You hold a high bar on quality and candidate experience at the same time<\/li>\n<li>You communicate directly and work well across partner organizations with different systems and cultures<\/li>\n<li>You care about the mission: expanding who gets to build with AI, and doing right by the people you employ<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>What success looks like<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each cohort is screened and hired on time, at target size, without cutting corners on signal quality<\/li>\n<li>The employment lifecycle runs cleanly: offers, onboarding, payroll, and benefits land on time and compliant across every state we hire in<\/li>\n<li>Cost and hours per fellow hired and onboarded drop cohort over cohort, because the work got automated and not because the team absorbed it<\/li>\n<li>Performance and ER issues get handled early, documented consistently, and resolved with the program manager rather than around them<\/li>\n<li>The pod grows in capability and ownership as the program scales, and the fractional support model either scales with it or you make the case for what replaces it<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Full-Time Employee Benefits<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>This is a 100% remote position—work from anywhere in the U.S.! CodePath prioritizes employee well-being with a competitive benefits package to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Health &amp; Wellness: Medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-covered for employees and dependents), employer-funded healthcare reimbursement, FSAs, and Employee Assistance Program<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p>Financial Security: 401(k), employer-paid life &amp; disability insurance, and identity theft protection<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p>Work-Life Balance: Generous PTO, paid holidays, 10 weeks of fully paid parental leave, and an annual year-end company closure (Dec 24 – Jan 2)<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p>Professional Growth: $1,000 annual professional development stipend and home office setup support<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p>​​Student Loan Forgiveness: CodePath is a qualifying employer for Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF), helping employees manage student loan debt<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p>Additional Perks: Pet wellness plans, legal services, home\/auto insurance discounts, and exclusive marketplace savings<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Pay range<\/p>\n<p>$110,000—$150,000 USD<\/p>","pubDate":"2026-09-01T05:14:59+00:00","salaryMin":110000,"salaryMax":150000,"salaryCurrency":"USD","salaryPeriod":"yearly"},{"id":152445,"url":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/jobs\/152445-digital-success-strategy-manager","jobSlug":"152445-digital-success-strategy-manager","jobTitle":"Digital Success Strategy Manager","companyName":"Jamf","companyLogo":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/data\/server-nyc0409\/galaxy\/mercury\/2025\/06\/6ac94784-221.jpg","jobIndustry":["Customer Support & Success"],"jobType":["Full-Time"],"jobGeo":"USA","jobLevel":"Any","jobExcerpt":"At Jamf, we believe in an open, flexible culture based on respect and trust. Our track record and thriving work environment all stem from the freedom we grant ourselves to get the job done right. We take pride in helping tens of thousands of customers around the globe succeed with Apple. The secret to our&hellip;","jobDescription":"<p>At Jamf, we believe in an open, flexible culture based on respect and trust. Our track record and thriving work environment all stem from the freedom we grant ourselves to get the job done right. We take pride in helping tens of thousands of customers around the globe succeed with Apple.<\/p>\n<p>The secret to our success lies in our connectivity, while operating with a high degree of flexibility. Work-life balance remains our priority while feeling connected is important to maintain our strong culture, achieve our goals, and thrive as #OneJamf.<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><strong>What you'll do at Jamf<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>At Jamf, we empower people to be their best selves and do their best work. The Digital Success Strategy Manager owns Jamf’s digital customer success strategy: the one-to-many, technology-led engagement model that drives adoption, retention, and value at scale. Building on deep digital-success expertise, the role designs a modernized, AI-powered evolution of that motion and defines what it should do and why. It partners with a Digital Success Engineer who builds the supporting automation and tooling, and it owns the adoption and retention outcomes the strategy delivers.<\/p>\n<p><strong>What you can expect to do in this role:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Owns the digital customer success strategy: the segmentation, lifecycle, and one-to-many engagement model that delivers adoption, retention, and value to customers outside high-touch coverage.<\/li>\n<li>Designs and leads a modernized, AI-powered evolution of the digital motion, identifying where AI, automation, and agents can scale proactive, personalized engagement and setting the roadmap to get there.<\/li>\n<li>Defines the strategy, requirements, and priorities that shape the digital motion’s tooling and automation, including the capabilities the Digital Success Engineer role must build. Partners closely with that role so the tooling serves the engagement model.<\/li>\n<li>Owns the adoption, retention, and coverage outcomes of the digital motion, defining the metrics and targets and iterating the strategy based on results.<\/li>\n<li>Designs digital engagement programs end to end, including customer journeys, campaigns, in-app guidance, and lifecycle touchpoints, in partnership with the Customer Success Management organization, Marketing, and Product.<\/li>\n<li>Partners with the Customer Success Analytics Engineer and data teams to ground the motion in customer health, adoption, and usage signals, so engagement is targeted by data rather than guesswork.<\/li>\n<li>Establishes governance and guardrails for automated customer communication, ensuring outreach is accurate, on-brand, appropriately reviewed, and safe to run at scale.<\/li>\n<li>Aligns cross-functional stakeholders (CSM, Marketing, Product, and Operations) around the digital success strategy and roadmap, building buy-in and driving adoption without direct authority.<\/li>\n<li>Serves as a subject-matter expert and internal advocate for digital and scaled customer success, bringing external best practices and a modernized vision to Customer Success leadership.<\/li>\n<li>Works with autonomy to execute the strategy and roadmap, exercising judgment on day-to-day priorities and escalating novel or highly cross-functional decisions for guidance.<\/li>\n<li>Other duties and special projects as assigned.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>What we are looking for:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>6+ years in customer success, digital or scaled customer success, or customer engagement strategy, including designing and running digital or one-to-many programs (required)<\/li>\n<li>Deep expertise in digital customer success: segmentation, lifecycle design, tech-touch engagement, and the tooling that powers it (required)<\/li>\n<li>Demonstrated ability to apply AI and automation to customer engagement, with a clear point of view on where AI scales the motion and experience putting it into practice (required)<\/li>\n<li>Experience translating strategy into clear requirements and priorities that a technical builder can execute against (required)<\/li>\n<li>Working knowledge of customer success data and metrics (adoption, customer health, gross and net retention) and how to use them to target and measure engagement (required)<\/li>\n<li>Familiarity with customer success and engagement platforms such as Gainsight, Salesforce, and in-app or digital-engagement tooling (preferred)<\/li>\n<li>Strong communication and cross-functional leadership skills, with the ability to influence CSM, Marketing, Product, and leadership stakeholders (required)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Education and Certifications<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bachelor’s degree in a business, technical, or related field, or equivalent experience (required)<\/li>\n<li>A combination of relevant experience and education may be considered (required)<\/li>\n<li>Certifications in relevant customer success, engagement, or data platforms (preferred<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>How we help you reach your best potential:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Named a 2025 Best Companies to Work For by U.S. News<\/li>\n<li>Named a 2025 Newsweek America’s Greatest Workplaces for Gen Z<\/li>\n<li>Named one of Forbes Most Trusted Companies in 2024<\/li>\n<li>Named a 2024 Newsweek America’s Greatest Workplaces for Parents &amp; Families<\/li>\n<li>Named a 2024 PEOPLE Companies That Care by PEOPLE® and Great Place To Work®<\/li>\n<li>We train and then we give you the room to grow. Our Jamfs can explore the vertical career path, as well as the horizontal, to discover new interests and opportunities.<\/li>\n<li>You don’t have to be a techie to be a Jamf. Our best-in-class sales focused Bootcamp training provides you with the technical and product knowledge required to confidently talk with customers about Jamf<\/li>\n<li>We set achievable targets, help each other out, and share best practices across the team.<\/li>\n<li>You will have the opportunity to make a real and meaningful impact for more than 75,000 global customers with the best Apple device management solution in the world<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Pay Transparency<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>At Jamf, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is set within a defined range. These ranges can vary based on hiring location. Where an individual's pay falls within that range depends on several factors, including role scope, location, budget, skills, experience, and qualifications. This approach helps ensure fair, competitive pay and provides room to grow as you develop in your role.<\/p>\n<p>For sales and commission-based roles, we post On-Target Earnings (OTE), which includes base salary plus estimated commission based on achieving 100% of performance targets. Commission is not guaranteed and varies based on individual performance results.<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p>The national pay transparency range below represents all U.S. locations and accounts for geographic differences in pay, resulting in a broader range. <\/p>\n<p>National Pay Transparency Range<\/p>\n<p>$104,000—$162,000 USD<\/p>\n<p><strong>What it means to be a Jamf?<br \/><\/strong>We are a team of free-thinkers, can-doers, and problem-crushers. We value humility and the relentless pursuit of knowledge. Our culture flows from a spirit of selflessness and relentless self-improvement - driving both personal growth and collective progress throughout our company. We unite around common goals while respecting personal approaches, believing that fulfilled individuals create a thriving, vibrant workplace. <\/p>\n<p>Our aim is simple: hire exceptionally good people who are incredibly good at what they do and let them do it. We provide the support and resources to let everyone be their authentic, best selves at work, at rest, and at play. We are committed to supporting the continual improvement of Apple in the workplace, the organizations that rely on them and the people who keep it all running smoothly. <\/p>\n<p>Above it all, waves our banner of #OneJamf – and the knowledge that when we stand together, we accomplish so much more than we could alone. We seek individuals who share this unwavering journey toward growth to join us in our quest for constant improvement. <\/p>\n<p><strong>What does Jamf do?<\/strong><strong><br \/><\/strong>Jamf extends the legendary Apple experience people enjoy in their personal lives to the workplace. We believe the experience of using a device at work or school should feel the same, and be as secure as, using a personal device. With Jamf, customers are able to confidently automate Mac, iPad, iPhone and Apple TV deployment, management, and security – anytime, anywhere – to protect the data and applications used by employees in the workplace, students learning in the classroom, and streamline communications in healthcare between patients and providers. More than 2,500 Jamf strong worldwide, we are free-thinkers, can-doers, and problems crushers who are encouraged to bring their whole selves to work each and every day.<\/p>\n<p>Get social with us and follow the conversation at #OneJamf<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><em>Jamf is committed to creating an inclusive &amp; supportive work environment for all candidates and employees. Candidates with disabilities or religious beliefs are encouraged to reach out if they need additional support or alternative options to our recruiting processes to accommodate their disability or religious belief. If you need an accommodation, please contact your Recruiter or Recruiting Coordinator directly. Requests for accommodation will be handled confidentially by Recruiting and will not be shared with the hiring manager. Jamf is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against individuals who request reasonable accommodation for disability or religious beliefs. To request accommodations please email us at <a href=\"mailto:recruiting@jamf.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">recruiting@jamf.com<\/a> <\/em><\/p><\/p>","pubDate":"2026-09-03T17:39:21+00:00","salaryMin":104000,"salaryMax":162000,"salaryCurrency":"USD","salaryPeriod":"yearly"},{"id":151516,"url":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/jobs\/151516-senior-technical-implementation-partner","jobSlug":"151516-senior-technical-implementation-partner","jobTitle":"Senior Technical Implementation Partner","companyName":"Qventus","companyLogo":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/data\/server-nyc0409\/galaxy\/mercury\/2022\/01\/0ad7e933ffa7b62281cc4b26710abfab.jpeg","jobIndustry":["Project & Program Management"],"jobType":["Full-Time"],"jobGeo":"USA","jobLevel":"Director","jobExcerpt":"On this journey for over 12 years, Qventus is leading the transformation of healthcare. We enable hospitals to focus on what matters most: patient care. Our innovative solutions harness the power of machine learning, generative AI, and behavioral science to deliver exceptional outcomes and empower care teams to anticipate and resolve issues before they arise.&hellip;","jobDescription":"<\/p>\n<p>On this journey for over 12 years, Qventus is leading the transformation of healthcare. We enable hospitals to focus on what matters most: patient care. Our innovative solutions harness the power of machine learning, generative AI, and behavioral science to deliver exceptional outcomes and empower care teams to anticipate and resolve issues before they arise.<\/p>\n<p>Our success in rapid scale across the globe is backed by some of the world's leading investors. At Qventus, you will have the opportunity to work with an exceptional, mission-driven team across the globe, and the ability to directly impact the lives of patients. We’re inspired to work with healthcare leaders on our founding vision and unlock world-class medicine through world-class operations. #LI-MB1<\/p>\n<\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Role<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>We’re looking for an experienced Senior Technical Implementation Partner - Inpatient Capacity to join our Delivery team. In this role, you will leverage your expertise in end-to-end delivery of technical features and functions to ensure successful and timely enterprise-scale software deployments. You’ll work cross-functionally with key leaders and users in the hospital including the executive sponsors, care coordinators, nurses, physicians, and IT Teams to shape solutions that deliver measurable value.<\/p>\n<p>This is a high-impact role that will influence our Inpatient Capacity solution, strengthen customer outcomes, and shape our company’s growth trajectory.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Key Responsibilities<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Define and manage the timeline for enterprise-wide, multi-module deployments, with an initial focus on the Qventus Inpatient Capacity solution.<\/li>\n<li>Work with Data Integration Specialists, Clinical Operation Consultants, and Product Specialists throughout each deployment to identify and implement solutions that deliver client value.<\/li>\n<li>Collaborate with external client teams to understand evolving requirements\/needs and communicate potential approaches to address them.<\/li>\n<li>Leverage deep functional Inpatient expertise to create and sustain buy-in from core users, executives, and care coordinators around workflows and tool adoption<\/li>\n<li>Provide technical project leadership to manage the full deployment lifecycle from internal project kickoff to go-live by prioritizing tasks, identifying dependencies, and ensuring deliverables are met.<\/li>\n<li>Build and manage relationships at multiple levels of client organizations, from frontline staff to C-suite stakeholders.<\/li>\n<li>Identify and mitigate risks and advise Delivery team leaders on project opportunities and risks, driving any issues to resolution.<\/li>\n<li>Identify process improvement opportunities and create structured approaches to close gaps.<\/li>\n<li>Serve as the owner and accountable team member for assigned accounts\/customers with limited oversight.<\/li>\n<li>Effectively lead complex engagements with matrixed teams (technical and operational).<\/li>\n<li>Articulate Qventus’ value proposition and create value for customers by establishing clearly defined business outcomes.<\/li>\n<li>Leverages deep functional expertise in order to sustain buy-in from core users and executives around workflows and tool adoption.<\/li>\n<li>Creates a customer base who is excited about Qventus and serves as a reference for prospective customers.<\/li>\n<li>A passion for fixing our healthcare system.<\/li>\n<li> <\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>What We’re Looking For<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>5+ years of experience in project\/program management experience with a comprehensive understanding of the business requirements and technical capabilities needed for an enterprise-wide SaaS implementation.<\/li>\n<li>5+ years professional experience working at a top healthcare consulting firm, digital health company, or health system.<\/li>\n<li>5+ years working cross-functionally with multiple teams, both internally &amp; externally, to manage end-to-end project lifecycles and to drive project milestones to completion.<\/li>\n<li>Previous experience working with Epic integrations and build. Specifically certification in IP Orders, IP ClinDoc, Ambulatory or related modules\/applications.<\/li>\n<li>Proven track record in applying strong quantitative and analytical skills in prior hospital systems (eg. EHR implementations) and project management with complex implementations in the provider-side health setting.<\/li>\n<li>Deep domain knowledge in Inpatient metrics, processes, challenges, and solutions; ability to engage in strategic\/operational discussions with hospital leaders and surgeons<\/li>\n<li>Strong communicator with the ability to influence and collaborate across all levels.<\/li>\n<li>Hands-on experience and proficiency with tools such as data validation dashboards, interpreting JAVA\/SQL code, complex Excel functions, etc.<\/li>\n<li>A systems thinker who balances big-picture vision with attention to detail.<\/li>\n<li>Passion for real-world impact and solving meaningful problems.<\/li>\n<li>Ability to travel up to 25%-30%<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Bonus Points For<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience with writing SQL queries (highly desired).<\/li>\n<li>Experience with HL7\/FHIR integrations.<\/li>\n<li>Experience working with clinical and\/or process consultants.<\/li>\n<li>PMP Certification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Compensation for this role is based on market data and takes into account a variety of factors, including location, skills, qualifications, and prior relevant experience. Salary is just one part of the total rewards package at Qventus. We also offer a range of benefits and perks, including Open Paid Time Off, paid parental leave, professional development, wellness and technology stipends, a generous employee referral bonus, and employee stock option awards.<\/p>\n<p>Salary Range<\/p>\n<p>$140,000—$160,000 USD<\/p>\n<p> Qventus values diversity in its workforce and proudly upholds the principles of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.ada.gov\/resources\/disability-rights-guide\/#:~:text=The%20ADA%20prohibits%20discrimination%20on%20the%20basis\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\"> Equal Opportunity Employment <\/a>. We welcome all qualified applicants and ensure fair consideration for employment without discrimination based on any legally protected characteristics, including, but not limited to: veteran status, uniformed service member status, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation and related medical conditions), national origin or ancestry, citizenship or immigration status, physical or mental disability, genetic information (including testing and characteristics) or any other category protected by federal, state or local law (collectively, \"protected characteristics\"). Our commitment to equal opportunity employment applies to all persons involved in our operations and prohibits unlawful discrimination by any employee, including supervisors and co-workers. <\/p>\n<p> Qventus participates in the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.e-verify.gov\/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">E-Verify<\/a> program as required by law and is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities in compliance with <a href=\"https:\/\/www.ada.gov\/resources\/disability-rights-guide\/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)<\/a>. In compliance with the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.oag.ca.gov\/privacy\/ccpa\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA)<\/a>, Qventus provides transparency into how applicant data is processed during the application process. Candidate information will be treated in accordance with our candidate privacy notice. <\/p>\n<p> *Benefits and perks are subject to plan documents and may change at the company's discretion. <\/p>\n<p> *Employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of our pre-employment background investigation and drug test. <\/p>","pubDate":"2026-08-24T17:45:22+00:00","salaryMin":140000,"salaryMax":160000,"salaryCurrency":"USD","salaryPeriod":"yearly"},{"id":149238,"url":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/jobs\/149238-lead-cloud-platform-dev-ops-engineer","jobSlug":"149238-lead-cloud-platform-dev-ops-engineer","jobTitle":"Lead Cloud Platform & Dev Ops Engineer","companyName":"University of Colorado","companyLogo":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/data\/server-nyc0409\/galaxy\/mercury\/2025\/09\/491790f6-221.jpeg","jobIndustry":["DevOps & Infrastructure"],"jobType":["Full-Time"],"jobGeo":"USA","jobLevel":"Senior","jobExcerpt":"Lead Cloud Platform &amp; Dev Ops Engineer - 40286 University Staff Description Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a&hellip;","jobDescription":"<div>Lead Cloud Platform &amp; Dev Ops Engineer - 40286 <\/div><div>University Staff <\/div><div><h2><div>Description<\/div><\/h2> <p><strong>Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education!<\/strong><\/p><p> <\/p><p>At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. <\/p><p> <\/p><p>By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cu.edu\/cu-careers\/cu-system\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Learn more about CU System Administration<\/a>.<\/p><p> <\/p><p><strong>Position Summary:<\/strong><\/p><p>University Information Services (UIS) provides technical services and enterprise applications to the University of Colorado campuses and the Office of the President. UIS is committed to delivering reliable, secure, and scalable technology solutions that support academic, administrative, and research functions.<\/p><p>The Lead Cloud Platform &amp; DevOps Engineer is responsible for leading the design, implementation, and support of cloud-based platforms and DevOps practices that enable consistent and efficient delivery of applications and services. This role focuses on cloud platform architecture, infrastructure automation, CI\/CD processes, system integration, and operational reliability.<\/p><p>This position supports the development and adoption of platform engineering practices, including infrastructure-as-code, containerization, and monitoring\/observability solutions. The role also contributes to the implementation of automation and data-driven technologies, including support for machine learning and intelligent automation workloads, in alignment with institutional standards and requirements.<\/p><p>The Lead Cloud Platform &amp; DevOps Engineer collaborates with campus IT teams, information security, and other stakeholders to implement platform solutions that meet security, compliance, and operational needs. Responsibilities include supporting service reliability practices, contributing to technical standards and documentation, and assisting with the evaluation and adoption of new tools and technologies.<\/p><p>This position provides technical guidance to development and operations teams, supports onboarding and enablement efforts, and contributes to continuous improvement of platform services. The role works across multiple projects and technical environments, supporting consistent implementation of DevOps and cloud engineering practices.<\/p><p>This position reports to the Assistant Director of Integrations Platform and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff system.<\/p><p><strong>Where You Will Work:<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration.<\/strong><\/p><p>This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado.<\/p><p><strong>Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented.<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Equal Opportunity Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. <\/p><p><strong>Duties and Responsibilities:<\/strong><\/p><p>Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to:<\/p><p>Platform Architecture, Engineering &amp; Delivery (60%)<\/p><ul><li>Design, implement, and maintain cloud platform architecture, including security, identity, networking, and policy controls aligned with institutional standards <\/li><li>Design, implement, and maintain CI\/CD pipelines and release processes, including build, testing, security, and deployment workflows across development and production environments <\/li><li>Support system integration across cloud and enterprise environments <\/li><li>Drive adoption of platform engineering practices, including containerization and automation <\/li><li>Contribute to automation and data-driven technologies, including support for machine learning and intelligent automation workloads <\/li><li>Work across multiple projects and technical environments to ensure consistent implementation of DevOps and cloud engineering practices <\/li><\/ul><p>Reliability, Security &amp; Operations (20%)<\/p><ul><li>Support platform reliability and operational practices, including defining service performance metrics (e.g., SLOs\/SLIs), implementing monitoring and observability solutions, and participating in incident response and disaster recovery activities <\/li><li>Collaborate with information security and compliance teams to implement and maintain platform security controls, access management, and data protection measures in alignment with regulatory requirements (e.g., FERPA, HIPAA) <\/li><li>Monitor and optimize platform performance, capacity, and cost utilization across cloud environments, ensuring consistency across environments <\/li><li>Ensure operational reliability and performance of platform services <\/li><li>Align platform solutions with institutional standards, policies, and requirements <\/li><\/ul><p>Leadership, Enablement &amp; Continuous Improvement (20%)<\/p><ul><li>Provide technical guidance and support to development and operations teams through documentation, training, and onboarding to promote effective use of platform services and<\/li><li>DevOps practices <\/li><li>Evaluate and implement new technologies and tools to support cloud platform capabilities, automation, data integration, and data-driven initiatives in collaboration with internal stakeholders <\/li><li>Contribute to development of technical standards, documentation, and governance practices <\/li><li>Contribute to continuous improvement of platform services and engineering processes<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>What We Offer:<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Salary:<\/strong> The anticipated hiring range has been established at <strong>$121,791.28<\/strong>.<\/p><p>CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees.<\/p><p> <\/p><p><strong>Benefits: <\/strong>With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness.<\/p><p> <\/p><ul><li><p>No-cost or low-cost medical &amp; dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break.<\/p><\/li><li><p>6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood.<\/p><\/li><li><p>A tuition benefit program for you and\/or your dependents.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Many additional perks &amp; programs with the CU Advantage.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p> <\/p><p>Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>For more information on benefits programs, please review our <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cu.edu\/node\/183087\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Comprehensive Benefits Guide<\/a>.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>Access our Total Compensation <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cu.edu\/node\/153125\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Calculator<\/a> to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position)<\/p><p> <\/p><p><strong>Qualifications:<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Minimum Qualifications:<\/strong><\/p><p>Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role.<\/p><ul><li>Master's degree in Computer Science, Computer or Electrical Engineering, or related IT field plus three (3) years of progressively responsible professional experience as a Platform Engineer (or a similar position) supporting production systems<br>or<\/li><li>A Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer or Electrical Engineering, or related IT field plus five (5) years of progressively responsible experience as a Platform Engineer (or a similar position) supporting production systems<\/li><li>Professional experience must include:<ul><li>Three (3) years of experience in:<ul><li>programming languages such as Python and\/or Java, including with machine learning frameworks;<\/li><li>leading or supporting DevOps initiatives, including implementation of CI\/CD pipelines, infrastructure-as-code, and release\/change management practices;<\/li><li>designing, developing, and maintaining cloud-based solutions using public cloud platforms (e.g. AWS services such as EKS, ECS, or Lambda), including containerized or serverless applications in production environments; and<\/li><li>implementing monitoring, logging, and reliability practices and supporting incident response using industry tools (e.g. Prometheus, Grafana, etc.)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Two (2) years of experience in:<ul><li>artificial intelligence and<\/li><li>enterprise IT and cloud environments, including API and integration development, streaming technologies (e.g. Kafka or RabbitMQ) and<\/li><li>collaboration with security or compliance stakeholders in support of technical controls<br> <\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><p><strong>How to Apply:<\/strong><\/p><p>For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: <\/p><ol><li>A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position.<\/li><li>A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting.<\/li><\/ol><p> <\/p><p>Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation.<\/p><p><strong>When to Apply:<\/strong><\/p><p>For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by <strong>August 14, 2026<\/strong>. Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>*Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. *<\/p><p><strong>Sponsorship Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position.<\/p><p><strong>Background Check Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and\/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment.<\/p><p><strong>ADA Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: <a href=\"mailto:systemhr@cu.edu\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">systemhr@cu.edu<\/a>. <\/p><p> <\/p> <\/div><div><\/div><div> <\/div><div><div><\/div><div><\/div> Application Materials Required: Resume\/CV <div><\/div><div><\/div> <\/div><div><h2>Job Category<\/h2>: Information Technology <\/div><div><h2>Primary Location<\/h2>: Denver <\/div><div>Department: S0001 -- System Administration - 50119 - University InformationServices <\/div><div><h2>Schedule<\/h2>: Full-time <\/div><div><h2>Posting Date<\/h2>: Jul 12, 2026 <\/div><div><h2>Unposting Date<\/h2>: Aug 15, 2026, 5:59:00 AM <\/div><div>Posting Contact Name: System HR Recruiting <\/div><div>Posting Contact Email: systemhr.recruiting@cu.edu <\/div><div>Position Number: 00705895<\/div>","pubDate":"2026-08-14T04:45:07+00:00","salaryMin":121791,"salaryMax":121791,"salaryCurrency":"USD","salaryPeriod":"yearly"},{"id":149240,"url":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/jobs\/149240-lead-cloud-platform-dev-ops-engineer-2","jobSlug":"149240-lead-cloud-platform-dev-ops-engineer-2","jobTitle":"Lead Cloud Platform & Dev Ops Engineer","companyName":"University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus","companyLogo":"https:\/\/jobicy.com\/data\/server-nyc0409\/galaxy\/mercury\/2026\/06\/52ccfc21-221.webp","jobIndustry":["DevOps & Infrastructure"],"jobType":["Full-Time"],"jobGeo":"USA","jobLevel":"Senior","jobExcerpt":"Lead Cloud Platform &amp; Dev Ops Engineer(Job Number: 40286)Description Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a&hellip;","jobDescription":"<div>Lead Cloud Platform &amp; Dev Ops Engineer(<h2>Job Number:<\/h2> 40286)<\/div><div><p><\/p><\/div><div><h2><div>Description<\/div><\/h2> <p><strong>Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education!<\/strong><\/p><p> <\/p><p>At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. <\/p><p> <\/p><p>By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cu.edu\/cu-careers\/cu-system\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Learn more about CU System Administration<\/a>.<\/p><p> <\/p><p><strong>Position Summary:<\/strong><\/p><p>University Information Services (UIS) provides technical services and enterprise applications to the University of Colorado campuses and the Office of the President. UIS is committed to delivering reliable, secure, and scalable technology solutions that support academic, administrative, and research functions.<\/p><p>The Lead Cloud Platform &amp; DevOps Engineer is responsible for leading the design, implementation, and support of cloud-based platforms and DevOps practices that enable consistent and efficient delivery of applications and services. This role focuses on cloud platform architecture, infrastructure automation, CI\/CD processes, system integration, and operational reliability.<\/p><p>This position supports the development and adoption of platform engineering practices, including infrastructure-as-code, containerization, and monitoring\/observability solutions. The role also contributes to the implementation of automation and data-driven technologies, including support for machine learning and intelligent automation workloads, in alignment with institutional standards and requirements.<\/p><p>The Lead Cloud Platform &amp; DevOps Engineer collaborates with campus IT teams, information security, and other stakeholders to implement platform solutions that meet security, compliance, and operational needs. Responsibilities include supporting service reliability practices, contributing to technical standards and documentation, and assisting with the evaluation and adoption of new tools and technologies.<\/p><p>This position provides technical guidance to development and operations teams, supports onboarding and enablement efforts, and contributes to continuous improvement of platform services. The role works across multiple projects and technical environments, supporting consistent implementation of DevOps and cloud engineering practices.<\/p><p>This position reports to the Assistant Director of Integrations Platform and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff system.<\/p><p><strong>Where You Will Work:<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration.<\/strong><\/p><p>This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado.<\/p><p><strong>Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented.<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Equal Opportunity Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. <\/p><p><strong>Duties and Responsibilities:<\/strong><\/p><p>Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to:<\/p><p>Platform Architecture, Engineering &amp; Delivery (60%)<\/p><ul><li>Design, implement, and maintain cloud platform architecture, including security, identity, networking, and policy controls aligned with institutional standards <\/li><li>Design, implement, and maintain CI\/CD pipelines and release processes, including build, testing, security, and deployment workflows across development and production environments <\/li><li>Support system integration across cloud and enterprise environments <\/li><li>Drive adoption of platform engineering practices, including containerization and automation <\/li><li>Contribute to automation and data-driven technologies, including support for machine learning and intelligent automation workloads <\/li><li>Work across multiple projects and technical environments to ensure consistent implementation of DevOps and cloud engineering practices <\/li><\/ul><p>Reliability, Security &amp; Operations (20%)<\/p><ul><li>Support platform reliability and operational practices, including defining service performance metrics (e.g., SLOs\/SLIs), implementing monitoring and observability solutions, and participating in incident response and disaster recovery activities <\/li><li>Collaborate with information security and compliance teams to implement and maintain platform security controls, access management, and data protection measures in alignment with regulatory requirements (e.g., FERPA, HIPAA) <\/li><li>Monitor and optimize platform performance, capacity, and cost utilization across cloud environments, ensuring consistency across environments <\/li><li>Ensure operational reliability and performance of platform services <\/li><li>Align platform solutions with institutional standards, policies, and requirements <\/li><\/ul><p>Leadership, Enablement &amp; Continuous Improvement (20%)<\/p><ul><li>Provide technical guidance and support to development and operations teams through documentation, training, and onboarding to promote effective use of platform services and<\/li><li>DevOps practices <\/li><li>Evaluate and implement new technologies and tools to support cloud platform capabilities, automation, data integration, and data-driven initiatives in collaboration with internal stakeholders <\/li><li>Contribute to development of technical standards, documentation, and governance practices <\/li><li>Contribute to continuous improvement of platform services and engineering processes<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>What We Offer:<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Salary:<\/strong> The anticipated hiring range has been established at <strong>$121,791.28<\/strong>.<\/p><p>CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees.<\/p><p> <\/p><p><strong>Benefits: <\/strong>With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness.<\/p><p> <\/p><ul><li><p>No-cost or low-cost medical &amp; dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break.<\/p><\/li><li><p>6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood.<\/p><\/li><li><p>A tuition benefit program for you and\/or your dependents.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office.<\/p><\/li><li><p>Many additional perks &amp; programs with the CU Advantage.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p> <\/p><p>Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>For more information on benefits programs, please review our <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cu.edu\/node\/183087\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Comprehensive Benefits Guide<\/a>.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>Access our Total Compensation <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cu.edu\/node\/153125\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Calculator<\/a> to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position)<\/p><p> <\/p><p><strong>Qualifications:<\/strong><\/p><p><strong>Minimum Qualifications:<\/strong><\/p><p>Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role.<\/p><ul><li>Master's degree in Computer Science, Computer or Electrical Engineering, or related IT field plus three (3) years of progressively responsible professional experience as a Platform Engineer (or a similar position) supporting production systems<br>or<\/li><li>A Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer or Electrical Engineering, or related IT field plus five (5) years of progressively responsible experience as a Platform Engineer (or a similar position) supporting production systems<\/li><li>Professional experience must include:<ul><li>Three (3) years of experience in:<ul><li>programming languages such as Python and\/or Java, including with machine learning frameworks;<\/li><li>leading or supporting DevOps initiatives, including implementation of CI\/CD pipelines, infrastructure-as-code, and release\/change management practices;<\/li><li>designing, developing, and maintaining cloud-based solutions using public cloud platforms (e.g. AWS services such as EKS, ECS, or Lambda), including containerized or serverless applications in production environments; and<\/li><li>implementing monitoring, logging, and reliability practices and supporting incident response using industry tools (e.g. Prometheus, Grafana, etc.)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Two (2) years of experience in:<ul><li>artificial intelligence and<\/li><li>enterprise IT and cloud environments, including API and integration development, streaming technologies (e.g. Kafka or RabbitMQ) and<\/li><li>collaboration with security or compliance stakeholders in support of technical controls<br> <\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><\/li><\/ul><p><strong>How to Apply:<\/strong><\/p><p>For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: <\/p><ol><li>A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position.<\/li><li>A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting.<\/li><\/ol><p> <\/p><p>Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation.<\/p><p><strong>When to Apply:<\/strong><\/p><p>For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by <strong>August 14, 2026<\/strong>. Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position.<\/p><p> <\/p><p>*Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. *<\/p><p><strong>Sponsorship Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position.<\/p><p><strong>Background Check Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and\/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment.<\/p><p><strong>ADA Statement:<\/strong><\/p><p>We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: <a href=\"mailto:systemhr@cu.edu\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\">systemhr@cu.edu<\/a>. <\/p><p> <\/p><\/div><div><\/div><div><div><\/div><div><\/div> Application Materials Required: Resume\/CV <div><\/div><div><\/div> <\/div><div><h2>Primary Location<\/h2>: Denver <\/div><div>Department: S0001 -- System Administration - 50119 - University InformationServices <\/div><div><h2>Schedule<\/h2>: Full-time <\/div><div><h2>Job Posting<\/h2>: Jul 12, 2026 <\/div><div><h2>Unposting Date<\/h2>: Aug 15, 2026, 5:59:00 AM <\/div><div>Posting Contact Name: System HR Recruiting <\/div><div>Posting Contact Email: systemhr.recruiting@cu.edu <\/div><div>Position Number: 00705895<\/div>","pubDate":"2026-08-14T04:45:04+00:00","salaryMin":121791,"salaryMax":121791,"salaryCurrency":"USD","salaryPeriod":"yearly"}],"statusCode":200,"success":true}